At Wed, 15 May 2013 18:58:06 +0200,
Jordi Mallach wrote:
> 
> If /proc/asound is not found, throw a warning and continue without
> any wrapping.

The purpose of aoss is to make OSS apps working *transparently*.
So spewing a warning at each time is a bad idea, IMO.

If a warning is justified, why don't you give a joyful success message
at each time if aoss can wrap the call? :)


Takashi

